  "slug": "learning-biology-small-c2ee",
  "summary": "Pocket-, pharmacophore- and objective-conditioned generators now pair with exposure-, toxicity- and pose-ranking evaluators that reorder which designs survive.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is conditioning generative models on explicit structural or functional constraints rather than unconditional sampling. PharmaDiff conditions a transformer diffusion model on pharmacophores for 3D ligand generation; PFM introduces a perturbed conditional probability path for pocket-conditioned flow matching, reporting Vina -7.12 on CrossDocked; CupOFMoCA enforces cross-component chemical constraints in discrete flows for PROTAC and peptide-drug conjugate assembly. On the protein side, Pallatom2 models sequence, backbone, side chains and target contacts atom-to-atom at 65.9M parameters with reported experimental validation; PAMP projects a differentiable turnover objective onto single-residue substitutions; PULSE steers protein language models with paired-unit local activation vectors; PDZ-binding motifs are designed along directions in a shared affinity latent space. Evaluation is being reframed: PBPK simulations re-rank PARP1 candidates by dose-driven exposure, SF-GA imposes synthetic accessibility while escaping P-gp substrate prediction, and Pyrite benchmarks agentic cofolding pose ranking.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-16"
}
